      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "The Mile 9 was the last hot meal before the Cordon roadblock. When Route 9 closed, Rosa chalked CLOSED over the specials and walked her regulars to the church; the travellers who stayed tipped the tables, dragged booth cushions and plywood round the counter and made their stand behind it with the coffee, the pie and a box of candles. They bolted the pantry's delivery door, piled the kitchen door high and wedged the front doors with every chair they had. It held until the night something came through the booth window. The regulars are still on their stools and in their booths, waiting for service, and the cook never left the griddle. Two of them had shut themselves in the walk-in when the window went, and the trapper among them left his bear trap set in the gap at the end of the counter.",
